ove."}, {"turn": 29, "text": "G5 lost 10.8 points, taking Black from -16.2 to -27.0, two moves after F3 had already lost 11.4. The engine wanted J2 here. Black's wall on the right had grown, but the lead was nowhere near it."}, {"turn": 50, "text": "After Opus 5.5's A6 captured two stones on the left (Black's capture count went from 2 to 4), White answered A5, which lost 65.8 points and moved Black from -54.1 to +11.7. It was the opponent's worst move, and it put Black clearly ahead."}, {"turn": 51, "text": "With a +11.7 lead, Opus 5.5 played E2, which lost 19.6 points and sent the score to -8.0. The engine's choice was H2. This is where the won position slipped away."}, {"turn": 57, "text": "B1 lost 50.8 points, from -8.4 to -59.3, and the engine's choice was H8. Moves 59, 61 and 63 each lost about 52 points as well, while the engine's choice stayed H8. White finally played it at move 64, and Black resigned at -62.9 or so after a few more moves."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py and count.py only parse a pasted board and report group liberties and an area count of the current position, and the other commands just read or append to games.md; nothing loops over candidate moves or plays continuations forward.", "stop": false}}